 "notes": [
  "No zonal office address and no hospital/UPHC table in this zone's appendix.",
  "Conservancy supervisor Unit-22 has two different numbers: 9445190422 (Solid Waste Management table, p.479) and 9445190606 (TNSCB contact-details table, p.484). Both kept; U-21 and U-23 match across tables, so they were not duplicated.",
  "inundation_streets = the 29-row 'Water stagnated streets in the previous monsoon - heavy rain' table (pp.488-489). Pump capacity is blank for rows 5 (Konnur High Road), 9 (AD Block) and 11 (W Block). Disposal point is 'SWD' for every row. No depth or days-to-drain columns exist. Photo captions on p.489 say 'Ward 103, Purasaivakkam High Road' / 'Ward 103, Millers Road' whereas the table puts those streets in ward 100.",
  "Sewer-block table also gives manhole counts (total 30), not in the schema.",
  "Relief centres: intro says 11 centres with total capacity 8435, but the table lists 16 (capacities sum to 4450). Every row is Drinking water Yes, Toilets Yes, Cooking No. Contacts carry the printed abbreviations SI/AE/ARO with their responsibility; where the 'Evacuation' and 'Relief Materials' AE numbers are identical they were merged into one contact. Centre 9 (ward 101) lists AE (Evacuation) as 9600482735, which is also the SI number of centre 7, while its Relief-Materials AE is 9445190401; copied as printed. Centres 3 and 4 have an AE row with blank responsibility (same number as the Evacuation AE).",
  "The evacuation/relief map legend (p.498) lists 27 shelter IDs (R1-R11A) and evacuation areas (E1-E11A) with ward numbers that do not always match the table (e.g. R3 'CHS Vellala Street' ward 96, R11 'CMS Mc Nichols Road' ward 107). Shelters only in the legend: Kamalammal Thirumana Mandapam, MGR Colony Anganwadi, Old Age Home, Thiru Vi Ka Higher Sec School, Periakoodal Corporation School, Metha Nagar Hr Sec School, Corporation Middle School Aminjikarai, Amman Koil Mandapam, CMS Mc Nichols Road, CHHS Subbarayan Street, Anganwadi Samidosspuram, Lockma Nagar Church, Sathyasai nagar Church. Not added to relief_centres (no capacity/contacts).",
  "Evacuation table (2015 flood, 20,555 people) has a 'Ward No./Name' column; the name went into 'area'. Relief-centre cells in rows 1 and 5 end with an unmatched ')' as printed.",
  "Water-entered-houses intro says 27 spots (NEM 2015, 369 people, 29 pumps of 2-7.5 HP); table has 27 rows. Ward names in the 'Ward No./Name' column were dropped (ward number kept).",
  "Tree fall: the table has one row per ward with a comma-separated list of streets; split into one entry per street (15 ward rows became 108 entries). 'VP Colony Extn.,,' printed with a double comma. The ward/name pairs in this table look shifted relative to other tables (e.g. 99/Anna Nagar, 103/Kilpauk, 104/Purasaiwalkam, 106/MMDA Colony, 107/Aminjikarai, 108/Chetpet); ward numbers copied as printed. Intro: 138 trees/branches fell.",
  "Subways: table says Harrington Subway is ward 108 but the photo caption says 'Ward 107, Harrington Road Subway'.",
  "Sewage pumping stations: intro says 16, table lists 15 (total 34 pumps). The table gives motor HP and number of pumps, not MLD capacity, so capacity_mld is null. Osanakulam (104) and Gnana Vinayagar Koil Street (107) have 'Nil' pumps.",
  "Parks: 41 rows; the single 'Name / Location of the Park' column went into 'name', and the 'Ward Name' column into 'location'. Rows 9 and 10 are identical as printed.",
  "Rescue boat Assistant Engineers were also added to officials (designation annotated with the boat station). NDRF Commandant phone printed '04177 – 246594/246269'; second number recorded as 04177-246269 assuming the shared STD code.",
  "Not captured (no schema field): canals (Otteri Nullah, Virugambakkam canal, Coovum river), ponds/lakes, SWD lengths, TNSCB tenements (15, population 26,984), sewage pump motor details."
 ]
